fit
    did:        sizes a container to the sum of its members. Value picks the
                direction: height/down, width/across, both, text; no value
                follows the container's own across/down. Down adds member
                heights and takes the widest width; across the reverse. A
                member that itself has fit is fitted first (recursive).
    where:      Details.twk getFitSettings 266-282 (reads the value, sets
                fitAcross/fitDown/fitBoth/fitText); Control.twk fitSize
                103-162 (the arithmetic); called from Control layout 259-264,
                a pass of its own between setDetails and setFrame.
                Stuff/Sheet.rtn 49-82 repeats the reading for matrix rows.
    when:       layout -- its own pass, after every field's details are set
                and before any frame is placed.
    inherited:  no (wig%fit, own attribute only).
    leans on:   member width/height already known (fixed numbers); does not
                look at text. fit=text sets fitText and NOTHING reads it --
                fitSize has no text branch, so fit=text did nothing.
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant -- arithmetic over member sizes. fit=text
                would need font measure.
    lean:       keep; respell as a layout-pass action. Decide whether
                fit=text is wanted (it never worked) or dropped.

flex
    did:        almost nothing in layout: it forces across, and with down it
                writes flexDirection=column. Both are CSS flexbox words; the
                only other reader of flex is IncantForms/HTML/htmlTraits
                (display=flex, flex-direction). The layout code named "flex"
                (Control.twk flexLayout 165-240, setFlexDetails 815-833) is
                NOT driven by the flex attribute -- it is driven by
                contentVaries, which is set by across="*" or down="*" (a
                value on across/down: repeat the member template as many
                times as there is room, used with next= and a source).
    where:      Details.twk initialize 305-326. Bot/Details.twk 394-408 same.
    when:       layout (details set-up).
    inherited:  no.
    leans on:   the HTML transpiler; the templates use it on tableBody,
                tableLabel, tableRow.
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant.
    lean:       drop as a layout attribute (it is an HTML hint). The real
                mechanism worth keeping is the across="*"/down="*" repeater
                -- see the across/down row. Clay's guess that flex and
                valueless space are one mechanism: NO, measured -- flex is a
                flexbox hint and the repeater fills with copies, not space.

expander (with expandable, expanded)
    did:        a tree's open/closed marker. A member tagged expander gets
                its group set to the template expanded ("-") or expandable
                ("+") depending on whether its leaf's source has members and
                whether the leaf is expanded; a leaf with no members gets an
                empty marker.
    where:      Map.rtn setExpander 803-830; called by tREE (1300) and by the
                expandTree event action xPAND (Actions.twk 399-421).
                Templates: IncantForms/Controls/templates expandable/expanded.
    when:       layout (tree set-up) and event (after each expand/collapse).
    inherited:  no; finds leaf with findAttribute (walks parents).
    leans on:   tEMPLATEs registry, the tree / leaf / source machinery,
                expandTREE and cOLLAPSErow.
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant (it swaps a child's group); drawing is text.
    lean:       keep, as part of a tree form; respell as a kant action. It is
                not an attribute so much as a reserved member name.

