Table attributes, then the list and layout forms
=============================================================================

How the old GUI drew at all (needed for every style row below)
    ⚠ The reference copy and Bot draw by DIFFERENT roads, and neither is
    native drawing of the field tree:
        Groups/GUI   Layout.twk drawRect 119-155 lays out, then builds an
                     HTML page with a <canvas> (Control.twk makeCanvas 402,
                     jsDraw 953-1040 writes one drawBox(...) JS call per
                     field) and loads it into a WKWebView. Fonts, alignment,
                     margins, flex etc. go out as CSS through toCSS (915) and
                     the CSS / pROPERTIEs registries in
                     IncantForms/HTML/htmlTraits.
        Bot          Layout.twk drawRect 28-70 renders the laid-out tree to a
                     PDF (Bot/PDF.twk, 523 lines: drawRoundedBox, displayCell,
                     displayImage, displayPath, getFontFrom, setPDFfill /
                     setPDFstroke) and shows it in a PDFView. That is the
                     "print-driven layout" Tony's forms notes propose -- Bot
                     already did it, in 2021.
    Layout itself (Control layout, Details setFrame / checkStretch /
    setInnerBox / checkFit) is the same in both and is plain arithmetic.

tableBody / tableCell / tableHead / tableLabel / tableRow
    did:        nothing of their own -- each is a template in
                IncantForms/Controls/templates that merges a bundle:
                    tableBody   normalFont flex down="*"
                    tableCell   selectable=no style
                    tableHead   headerFont height=30 across
                    tableLabel  flex center selectable=no
                    tableRow    height=20 across flex style
                The only working parts are down="*" (the repeater, see
                across/down), height, across, selectable, and the font name.
                flex and center are CSS hints; bare `style` has no value, and
                Bot's sTYLE refuses a nameless style ("style attribute has to
                specify a name"); in Groups/GUI style is not mapped at all.
    where:      templates file; no C++ names them (searched Groups/GUI and
                Bot: zero hits).
    when:       define (template merge into the parent).
    inherited:  no (merged in, not inherited).
    leans on:   the template merge (old #registry tEMPLATEs + #macro).
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant.
    lean:       respell as kant templates (mergeContainers); drop flex,
                center and bare style from them.

list (the form, IncantForms/Windows/list)
    did:        a table of records whose attributes differ per record
                (listStuff): one row per record, and inside each row one
                cell per ATTRIBUTE of that record, tag on one line and value
                under it, the two lines scrolling together. The file's own
                ?...? comments explain it well and are accurate to Map.rtn.
                Machinery: source=listStuff (a Source over the block, kept in
                a hidden sRCe attribute); next=body (each row pulls the next
                record into row.group); source=row useNext useAttributes
                across="*" (a nested source over the CURRENT record's
                attributes, repeated across); tag / trait=source (show the
                attribute's tag, or its value); scrollWith (two blocks
                scroll as one).
    where:      Map.rtn sOURCE 933-1018, nEXT 541-622, tAG 1079-1121, tRAIT
                1207-1258, scrollWITH 706-741; Control.twk flexLayout and
                setFlexDetails (the repeater).
    when:       layout, then listener-driven on every scroll / source move.
    inherited:  sRCe is found with findAttribute -- the source is inherited
                down the tree; that is the whole mechanism.
    leans on:   Source (Source.twk), listeners, contentVaries / indexed
                flags, setFLEXcontent.
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant (the drawing is whatever cells use).
    lean:       keep the idea, respell small: source / next / trait / tag are
                the data-binding core of forms and A2's listener probe is
                their first question. useNext and useAttributes are modifiers
                worth renaming.

layout (the form, IncantForms/Windows/layout)
    did:        a showcase window with two cards: headed text, images, a
                button (action=fire prints "Fire action for <tag>"), wrapped
                text, a sorted table (source=phone, sort= on headings, key
                and trait cells, next=fifth), a popup=dialog box, form
                templates with $name/$content references, a pullDown=pull
                menu. It touches nearly every attribute in this file.
    where:      the form only; it names `phone` and `pull` and `dialog`,
                which it does not define (searched IncantForms: phone
                appears nowhere else) -- so it never ran whole as written.
    when:       all three moments.
    inherited:  -
    leans on:   everything: cards, popup, pullDown, form, source, next, key,
                trait, sort, image, text, rounded, border, fill, font.
    C++ floor:  window, draw, image, font measure.
    lean:       keep as the target showcase, but it is a destination, not
                A4's first light; rebuild it last.

cards
    did:        the members of a cards block are stacked; all are hidden
                (noRoom) but one -- the first, or the one named by
                cards=Name. Event action "card" (Actions.twk gotoCARD 64-91)
                switches; scrollCards (Details.rtn 191) steps with the
                arrow keys / scroll.
    where:      Map.rtn setCARD 764-800; Details initialize 323 (orient =
                cards), setFrame 573-577 (each card gets the full box).
    when:       layout; event to switch.
    inherited:  no.
    leans on:   noRoom.
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant.
    lean:       keep, respell.

across / down (and the "*" repeater)
    did:        orientation of the members. A count value (across=3) repeats
                the block that many times. Any other value (across="*")
                sets contentVaries: the members become a template (kept in a
                hidden vCONTENt) and are copied as many times as fit, each
                copy pulling its record with next=. Neither given: down,
                unless flex.
    where:      Details initialize 310-326; Control.twk setDetails 779-814,
                flexLayout 165-238, setFlexDetails 815-833,
                resetVariableContent 762-777.
    when:       layout; the repeater re-runs on resize and scroll.
    inherited:  no.
    leans on:   next / source, item heights or widths (a repeated member
                without a fixed height is a fatal error: exit(0)).
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant.
    lean:       keep across/down; keep the repeater but give it its own name
                (it is a value smuggled onto across/down -- one channel, two
                meanings).

space (special field)
    did:        NOTHING SPECIAL -- no code names it (searched Groups/GUI and
                Bot for space as a word: only a character set in Groups.twk).
                Its behaviour comes from the general rule: any member with
                no height (in down) or no width (in across) gets an equal
                share of what the fixed members leave (Details checkStretch
                141-187, setFrame 548-552). So every unsized field is a
                "space"; space is just the conventional name for an empty one.
    where:      Details.twk checkStretch, setFrame.
    when:       layout.
    inherited:  no.
    leans on:   -
    C++ floor:  none, pure kant.
    lean:       keep as is; vertical align by space works already.
    note:       checkStretch's percent arm adds detail.height * n / 100,
                the member's own height rather than the parent's -- looks
                wrong; recorded here only, not chased.
